  "anomaly_detected": false,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [],
  "summary": "Every component I can read off the drawing matches the specification: SKW92A module, BBQ10KBD keyboard, NTR2101P high-side display switch with a 10 k gate pull-up, MCH3478 boost MOSFET, three SS2040FL charge-pump diodes plus the SS2040FL battery-isolation diode, 10 uH boost inductor, 0.47 ohm current-sense resistor, 1 uF/6.3 V and 1 uF/25 V EPD caps, FH34SRJ-24S FPC, FAN53610AUC33X with 2.2 uF/10 uF in/out caps and the 1.0 uH LQM2MPN1R0MGHL inductor, Keystone 1043 cell, 1825232-1 reset switch, RJ45, USB-A and barrel jack. The reference designators differ from the spec (e.g. U5->U10, U4->U11, Q2->Q3, Q1->Q2, R2->R1, R1->R2, J1->J5, J7->J2, J4->J6, J5->J8, J3->J10, IC1->IC2, L2->L1, L1->L3) but this is a consistent relabeling of a different build, not a behavioral deviation. The localized connections I can trace (HW_RESET switch to GND, debug UART TX/RX to the 3-pin header, SD VDD to +3V3, boost gate to the FPC GDR pin, sense resistor from MOSFET source to GND, regulator EN tied to VIN and MODE to GND, RJ45 now bridged to the module's LAN_PORT nets) are all consistent with the spec, and the spec's documented known issues (barrel-jack battery-disconnect behavior, the earlier display-MOSFET heating bug, the inferred bit-banged SPI) are explicitly not anomalies. The long cross-sheet bus traces are not legible at the supplied resolution, and no deviation in them is supported by the drawing, so I report no anomaly."
}

